+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool definitions already describe the JSON Schema sent to providers; the registry is the boundary that applies that schema before an executor can receive model-supplied input.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking its executor; a rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` whose result identifies the failing property and constraint without exposing submitted property values, including in registry log lines. ([validated by: rejects required, typed, and enum-invalid input before execution without exposing input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L20))
+- Schema-valid input reaches the executor exactly once and unchanged, including properties the schema does not declare. ([validated by: passes schema-valid input, including unknown keys, to the executor exactly once without rewriting it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57))
+- A static definition's schema is compiled during registration and reused for later calls, so an uncompilable schema names its tool at registration time; an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration, retains that compiled schema, and preserves unknown-tool errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79))
+- A function-valued tool definition resolves and validates against the schema current for each call rather than a prior resolved schema. ([validated by: resolves function-valued definitions for each call and validates the schema current for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L104))
+
+## Tool loop contract
+
+- A schema rejection is returned to the provider as a tool result, allowing a corrected retry to complete within the configured tool-round bound rather than rejecting the conversation. ([validated by: returns a rejected call to the provider so its corrected retry completes instead of rejecting the conversation](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L37))
